From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 tab sleep: a tab left alone is frozen before it is unloaded (ABI 1.71, bridge 0.83.0)

Darni unloaded a tab nobody had looked at for four hours and did nothing
before that: a tab in the background ran its timers and scripts at full
cost until it was discarded, and then had to load again. The best of the
other browsers freezes such a tab after thirty minutes: the page stays in
memory, its scripts and timers stop, and showing it resumes it at once.

What this patch does.

- ReArcTabFreeze(tab): the host asks that the tab's page be frozen. The
  bridge holds a performance_manager::freezing::FreezingVote for the tab's
  WebContents (FreezeHold, a WebContentsUserData in freeze_adapter.cc). The
  freezing is Chromium's own, FreezingPolicy with WebContents::SetPageFrozen:
  the page is frozen while every page of its browsing instance has a vote and
  none of Chromium's CannotFreezeReasons applies (visible, or visible in the
  last five minutes; audible, or audible in the last five; capturing camera
  or microphone; WebRTC; being mirrored; a Web Lock or IndexedDB lock; a USB,
  Bluetooth, HID or serial device; loading; notification permission; WebUI),
  and it thaws the moment one starts. OK means the request is held.
- What Chromium's policy does not know about a bridge tab, Freeze refuses
  (invalid_state): a tab that is presented or has visibility intent, is not
  hidden, is discarded, crashed, loading or without a committed entry, is
  being captured, is audible or has playing media (the bridge's media
  session state, heard or not), has picture-in-picture or fullscreen, an
  open permission request (PermissionRequestManager) or passkey request
  (AuthenticatorRequestScheduler), or a download of its own in progress.
  busy while a script or snapshot of the host's runs; unsupported for a
  hosted DevTools frontend and without a page node.
- The shared tab (security's advance read, 2). tab/102 keeps a tab that is
  shared while nobody looks at it hidden: its picture and its sound are
  hidden capturers, and its page node is not visible, so Chromium's policy
  would freeze it and the share would show a still picture. Freeze refuses a
  tab with any capturer (WebContents::IsBeingCaptured, hidden ones
  included), and ReArcDisplayCaptureRespond drops the request of the tab it
  is about to share (HostPicker::ShareTab) before the capture starts.
- The request ends, and the page thaws, when the tab is shown
  (OnVisibilityChanged to anything but hidden; content thaws a page that is
  made visible by itself), when it navigates to another document, starts
  media or becomes audible, enters picture-in-picture, is discarded, loses
  its renderer, is shared, is asked to close (a frozen page answers no
  beforeunload), when the host evaluates a script in it or sends a media
  action, and with ReArcTabUnfreeze. The host asks again when the tab has
  been left alone for its own time; a request never outlives a use of the
  tab.
- ReArcTabGetFreezeState(tab, &requested, &frozen): whether a request is
  held, and the page's lifecycle state as its renderer last reported it
  (PageNode::GetLifecycleState).
- Feature "tab_freeze", ABI 1.71, bridge 0.83.0. Three functions, no struct,
  no callback, no event.

Thawing (security's advance read, 3). The bridge queues nothing for a
frozen page, and neither does this patch: there is no list of things to do
at the thaw. A frozen page runs no task, so it asks for nothing: no dialog,
no pop-up, no download, no permission or notification request reaches the
browser process, and the host hears nothing of the tab. A request that was
open before the freeze keeps the tab from being frozen (above; the host
answers for its own prompts). At the thaw the page's own timers and
handlers run again, and what they ask then is a request of that moment,
treated as the same request of a tab that was never frozen: a pop-up
without a click is dropped and no tab is made for it (tab_adoption.cc; a
click cannot be younger than the five minutes the tab must have been
hidden, and activation lasts five seconds); a JavaScript dialog, a
download or a permission request from a timer is what a tab in the
background may ask at any time. The bridge adds no rule for those and
takes none away.

State. Nothing is persisted: no preference, no content setting, no file. A
vote lives in the browser process and ends with the tab.

Chromium's own freezing is otherwise as it was: its Battery Saver and
"infinite tabs" freezing are not turned on by this patch, and its discard
of frozen pages whose memory grows (FreezingDiscarder) takes tabs of a tab
strip only (DiscardEligibilityPolicy: kNotATab), which a bridge tab is not.

Tests: engine/tests/c_abi_freeze_host.mm (run_c_abi.py freeze). The runner
passes
--enable-features=CPUMeasurementInFreezingPolicy:freezing_visible_protection_time/1s/freezing_audio_protection_time/1s,
Chromium's own parameters, so a tab hidden a second ago can be frozen; a
release keeps the five minutes. Its window is off every screen, it sends no
input and its sound is muted. engine/tests/check_abi171_imports.py: the
struct layouts of 1.70 are unchanged, three functions are added, no struct
and no callback type. The shell's self-test step "tab freezing"
(ChromiumSelfTest.tabFreezeChecks) drives the same through the model.

Touches: the bridge only. New freeze_adapter.cc; one line each in
close_controller.cc, rearc_display_capture.cc and twice in
rearc_services_abi.cc; MediaIsPlaying in media_adapter.{h,cc};
rearc_abi_internal.h, rearc_engine_abi.{h,mm}, rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm,
chrome/browser/BUILD.gn, and the three names in chrome/app/framework.exports
and framework.order. No upstream file but those three lists.

Type-checked with the tree's clang (out/ReArc-codecs-arm64 flags, Chromium's
plugins, -fsyntax-only), then built in out/ReArc-codecs-arm64 on 2026-11-25:
overlay a3b96b217d, and the three names in framework.exports and
framework.order as a second overlay commit, 577e70cef2 (tab/105 was
committed between the two; this patch is the two together, on tab/102).

Run on that build (run_c_abi.py freeze, REARC_CHROMIUM_OUT the release out
dir, nothing on screen): a tab never shown is frozen and silent for three
seconds, and after Unfreeze it is the same document with one freeze and one
resume event and a longest gap of 4.2 s between two ticks of its timer; a
tab shown and hidden again is frozen after the protection second, thawed
by being shown and by a script of the host's; a tab that plays sound is
refused six times in a row and keeps ticking; a tab with a beforeunload
handler is frozen and its discard is refused, frozen or not; a frozen tab
without one is discarded; a frozen tab picked for a share has no request
when the answer returns, is live with 2 and then 13 frames, is refused
while shared and accepted after; a tab with a download in progress is
refused until it ends; the page that asks from a timer makes the host hear
nothing while frozen (0 pop-ups, 0 permission requests, 0 dialogs, 0
downloads), its timer runs 4.3 s late at the thaw, its pop-up makes no tab,
and its dialog and its download arrive then. The network audit shows
loopback only. Not run: the shell's self-test step, which needs the screen.

Last rebased: 2026-11-25 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.114 (overlay 86afa51467).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

