+// stays in memory with its scripts and timers stopped (page lifecycle
+// "frozen"); showing the tab resumes it at once, with no reload and no
+// event to the host. Freeze asks: OK means the request is held, not that the
+// page is frozen yet. Chromium freezes it while none of its own reasons not
+// to applies (visible, or visible in the last five minutes; audible, or
+// audible in the last five; camera, microphone, WebRTC, being mirrored; a Web
+// Lock or IndexedDB lock; a USB, Bluetooth, HID or serial device; loading;
+// notification permission; WebUI; and the same for every page of the same
+// browsing instance), and thaws it the moment one starts.
+// Freeze refuses, with invalid_state, a tab that is presented or has
